# NEVER CHANGE THE BEHAVIOR OF THE LEGACY IMPLEMENTATION

The C# `Tick*` paths (`TickDefault`, Bergania/Geranium ticks), `SeedAgent`, and other pre-graph plant logic are the **reference** the node graphs must match.

## Do not

- Edit legacy tick bodies, growth/lignify/chaining formulas, or ctor side effects to “fix” parity or visuals
- Change rhizome birth, wood, energy, or morphology so legacy runs differently than before
- “Improve” legacy while porting features — put new behavior only in graphs / graph config / graph interpreters

## Do

- Emulate legacy in **behavior graphs** and graph-side config resolution
- Keep `SpeciesMorphology.Resolve` (no-graphs / legacy) on the **old** replace-or-predefined path
- Build node-graph morphology from `behaviorConfiguration` via `SpeciesSettingsFromConfiguration` in `PlantSpeciesProfile`
- If legacy and graphs disagree, change the **graph** (or tests), not Tick*

## Exceptions

Only when the user **explicitly** asks to change legacy implementation behavior.
